<title>GERMANY: Berlin airports Feb passenger traffic down 8.9pct.</title>
<headline>Berlin airports Feb passenger traffic down 8.9pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Passenger traffic at the three Berlin airports, Tegel, Schoenefeld and Tempelhof, slumped 8.9 percent year-on-year to 728,068 travellers in February, the German airport association ADV said.</p>
<p>This followed a slight rise of 0.6 percent in January, the ADV monthly traffic report showed.</p>
<p>The following tables show 1997 passenger details with percentage changes on the same period 12 months ago.</p>
<p>    Feb 1997			Monthly total	Pct change</p>
<p>    Total				728,068	    Down  8.9</p>
<p>    Domestic			   402,427	    Down  9.4</p>
<p>    Europe			     267,441	    Down  6.7</p>
<p>    Overseas			    45,126	    Down 21.8</p>
<p>    Transit			     12,373	    Up   16.2</p>
<p>    Jan-Feb 1997		 Cumulative total    Pct change</p>
<p>    Total			    1,432,643	    Down  4.5</p>
<p>    Domestic			   789,802	    Down  6.0</p>
<p>    Europe			     528,365	    Down  0.6</p>
<p>    Overseas			    87,866	    Down 14.3</p>
<p>    Transit			     25,062	    Up    3.8</p>
<p>--Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom. Tel +44 171 542 7706; Fax: 5017</p>
</text>
